  ('goldfinch', 'Goldfinch', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'lending-markets', 'https://goldfinch.finance (goldfinch.finance)', ARRAY['Loan terms instantiated as Borrower Pool smart contracts', 'credit deployed to approved borrowers (docs.goldfinch.finance)']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "Private credit protocol that deploys stablecoin capital into borrower pools with onchain loan terms and repayment tracking. (docs.goldfinch.finance)", "extras": {"Collateral Types Supported ERC-20s; ETH; widely supports LST collateral in certain markets (risk-parameter dependent) ERC-20s; ETH (wrapped); selected stablecoins; LST support market-dependent (primarily via governance-approved assets) ETH; ERC-20s; selected LSTs; RWAs (via specialized vaults) ERC-20s + ETH (incl. stETH, DAI, sDAI at launch; asset set is governance/risk-managed) (TradingView) ERC-20s; market-defined collateral/loan pairs (including LSTs, stablecoins, and other ERC-20 collateral depending on market config) (docs.morpho.org)": "Primarily USDC-denominated loans with offchain collateral / legal recourse (not crypto overcollateral) (docs.goldfinch.finance)", "Dependency Concentration Risk High oracle reliance + large-collateral concentration risk (market-dependent); governance/parameter-change latency risk High oracle reliance; Medium–High asset concentration risk in v3 base asset; governance latency risk High oracle reliance; High governance concentration risk; Medium–High RWA dependency risk High oracle reliance + governance/parameter-change latency risk; asset concentration risk (DAI-centric design) (Spark Docs) High oracle dependence (per-market); configuration/parameter risk; integration/curation risk (markets can be permissionlessly created but quality varies) (mixbytes.io)": "High underwriting/servicer dependence; High offchain enforcement risk; borrower concentration risk", "Downstream Consumers Yield strategies, leveraged LPs, hedged carry, structured products, derivatives margin users Yield strategies, leveraged positions, DAO treasuries, arbitrage and carry strategies DEX liquidity, lending protocols, yield strategies, derivatives, DAOs, payment rails Yield strategies, stablecoin allocators, leverage users, structured products integrating DAI liquidity Vaults/allocators, structured lending products, leveraged strategies, institutional deployers using Morpho rails": "RWA/credit allocators; diversified stablecoin yield strategies; DAOs seeking private-credit yield", "Governance Model Token governance (AAVE) via Aave DAO processes; proposals/voting for parameter changes (aave.com) Token governance (COMP) via Compound DAO proposals and voting Token governance (MKR) with executive votes and onchain spell execution Governance via SPK token; Snapshot/signaling and governance system documented by Spark (Spark Docs) Token governance via MORPHO; weighted voting and defined governance powers (docs.morpho.org)": "GFI token governance (docs.goldfinch.finance)", "Historical Stress Events Yes (v1 largely frozen/disabled for new supply/borrow; legacy positions remain manageable) (messari.io) Yes (v2 experienced stress events and governance interventions; migration to v3 reflects risk simplification lessons) Yes (notably March 2020 “Black Thursday” auction failures; subsequent mechanism redesigns) No major protocol-loss event cited in core docs; treat as “monitor” (bug bounty active) (Immunefi) Yes (documented oracle-manipulation event on a specific market; plus a frontend-related incident where contracts unaffected) (Morpho Governance Forum)": "Yes (borrower defaults have been discussed in ecosystem risk coverage) (cork.tech)", "Interest Rate Model Utilization-based variable rates; also supports “stable” borrow rate mode (market-specific) Utilization-based interest rate curves per asset (v2); simplified rate model with base/borrow asset separation (v3) Governance-set stability fees per vault type (effectively interest rates) Utilization-based IR model (Aave v3 lineage) + custom DAI/sDAI strategies in Spark context (Medium) Market-selected Interest Rate Models (IRMs); IRMs/LLTVs are constrained by governance whitelists (docs.morpho.org)": "Interest and repayment schedules defined in borrower pool terms (contract-enforced accounting) (docs.goldfinch.finance)", "Isolation of Risk Risk primarily at market/reserve parameter level (not isolated per-user); isolation features exist in newer versions/markets but not “isolated pools” by default Moderate isolation: v3 introduces asset isolation via a single base asset with segmented collateral; v2 uses shared pools High isolation at vault-type level; each collateral type has independent parameters Shared pool risk by asset/reserve parameters (not per-market isolation like Morpho Blue) High isolation: each market is isolated and immutable by design (docs.morpho.org)": "High isolation per borrower pool (idiosyncratic credit risk per pool)", "Launch Year 2020 (v1 Ethereum mainnet) (aave.com) 2018 (v2 on Ethereum) 2017 (Single-Collateral DAI; Multi-Collateral DAI in 2019) 2023 (public launch May 9, 2023) (X (formerly Twitter)) 2023 (Morpho Blue introduced Oct 2023) (morpho.org)": "2021 (protocol active era; V1 docs cover mechanics)", "Lending Model Pooled liquidity markets (multi-asset) Pooled liquidity markets (v2); single-collateral base with isolated borrow assets (v3/Comet) CDP / Vault-based collateralized lending Pooled liquidity markets (Aave v3-derived money market) (Spark Docs) Permissionless, isolated lending markets (1 collateral + 1 loan asset per market) (docs.morpho.org)": "Permissioned / borrower-pool private credit (tranching: senior/junior)", "Liquidation Mechanism Onchain liquidations triggered when Health Factor < 1; liquidators repay debt for collateral + bonus (bonus/thresholds per asset, governance/risk-managed) (aave.com) Onchain liquidations when collateral value breaches borrow limits; liquidators repay debt for collateral at protocol-defined incentives Onchain liquidation via auctions (debt, collateral, surplus); keeper participation required Health Factor-based liquidations (HF < 1), onchain seizure/repay mechanics (Spark Docs) Standard liquidation when LTV exceeds LLTV; liquidators repay debt and seize collateral at discount (protocol-enforced) (docs.morpho.org)": "Hybrid default recovery: contracts track obligations; enforcement/liquidation can rely on offchain legal processes (research.nansen.ai)", "Maintaining Organization Aave DAO (governance) + Aave Labs (major dev & interface/operator tooling) (aave.com) Compound DAO (governance) with historical development by Compound Labs MakerDAO (DAO-governed protocol) with core units / contributors maintaining modules Spark Governance (SPK) operating via the Spark Agent in the Sky Atlas (Sky ecosystem) (Spark Docs) Morpho Governance (MORPHO token); governance whitelists IRMs/LLTVs and can activate fee switch (docs.morpho.org)": "Goldfinch governance via GFI; initial development referenced in dev docs as Warbler Labs (Goldfinch dev docs)", "Oracle Dependencies Primarily Chainlink price feeds with protocol risk controls (market-config dependent) Chainlink price feeds (primary), with protocol-defined fallbacks/guards Decentralized Oracle Network (Maker Oracles) with Chainlink integrations and redundancy Oracle-driven risk system; Spark has integrated oracle providers (e.g., RedStone) for lending markets (RedStone blog) Oracle per market; Morpho established an oracle wrapper for Chainlink feeds to support initial markets (morpho.org)": "Limited role vs. overcollateralized DeFi; borrower pools are not primarily oracle-liquidation driven", "Parameter Control Governance-gated risk parameters + emergency controls (typical DeFi risk-admin pattern) Governance-gated parameters; admin/guardian controls for emergencies (especially during upgrades) Fully governance-controlled parameters; emergency shutdown and circuit breakers exist Parameter updates controlled through governance actions on the Spark Agent (risk, budgets, onboarding, deployments) (Spark Docs) Governance whitelists key risk parameters (LLTVs, IRMs) and can toggle fee switch (capped) (docs.morpho.org)": "Governance influences protocol direction/parameters and onboarding frameworks; pool-level terms set per borrower proposal (docs.goldfinch.finance)", "Practitioner Validation Check YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation rules enforced by contracts (HF<1) (aave.com) • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced by contracts • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced via protocol auctions • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation rules enforced (HF<1) (Spark Docs) • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced (LTV>LLTV) (docs.morpho.org) • YES positions unwindable programmatically": "Credit creation: YES (borrower pool contracts) (docs.goldfinch.finance) • Liquidation enforcement: PARTIAL (often offchain legal) (research.nansen.ai) • Programmatic unwind: PARTIAL (depends on pool liquidity + recovery)", "Practitioner’s Note Research focus: liquidation mechanics (health factor dynamics), collateral mix concentration, oracle coverage/fallbacks, and governance latency during fast markets. Also track version/market fragmentation (v1 frozen vs v3 active) when analyzing risk. (messari.io) Research focus: differences between v2 and v3 risk profiles; base-asset concentration in v3; liquidation throughput under stress; governance response speed during incidents. Research focus: auction efficiency during stress, oracle latency, RWA exposure and offchain enforcement risk, governance concentration, and emergency shutdown assumptions. Watchpoints: Aave v3 fork deltas (custom DAI/sDAI logic), oracle stack and feed coverage, asset-list governance, and liquidation throughput under stablecoin stress. Also note Spark’s bug bounty posture. (Spark Docs) Watchpoints: oracle selection/config is a first-order risk surface (market-by-market). Validate LLTV choice, oracle robustness, and liquidation liquidity for collateral. Review post-mortems for oracle manipulation and operational incidents. (Morpho Governance Forum)": "Key diligence: this is not “Aave-style liquidation.” Validate (1) borrower screening, (2) legal enforceability, (3) recovery timelines, (4) concentration by borrower/pool, (5) liquidity/exit constraints. (research.nansen.ai)", "Primary Role in DeFi Base credit + leverage layer for Ethereum DeFi Base credit layer and leverage primitive for Ethereum DeFi Stablecoin issuance + base credit layer for DeFi DAI-centered credit & liquidity venue; major stablecoin + ETH collateral borrowing/supply rails inside Sky ecosystem (Blockworks) Base lending primitive for permissionless risk markets; “lending infrastructure” others build vaults/allocators on top of": "Bridge between DeFi capital and real-economy/private credit underwriting", "Protocol Status Active (v3 widely used; v1 largely frozen) (messari.io) Active (v3 “Comet” is primary; v2 largely deprecated/frozen for growth) Active (DAI issuance core to Ethereum DeFi) Active Active": "Active (product focus has evolved; protocol still used for onchain private credit) (docs.goldfinch.finance)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending; collateralized credit issuance; onchain interest rate mechanics; liquidation + solvency enforced by protocol logic. (aave.com) Meets criteria: issues credit onchain against collateral; defines interest rates, liquidation logic, and solvency rules fully in smart contracts. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing; collateralized credit issuance; explicit liquidation and solvency logic; interest (stability fees) set and enforced onchain. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending, collateralized credit issuance, onchain interest + liquidation + solvency rules. (Spark Docs) Meets criteria: creates credit and enforces liquidation/solvency fully onchain; interest and risk logic are protocol-defined per market. (docs.morpho.org)": "Meets Lending inclusion on onchain loan issuance + contractual repayment logic; note: default recovery is commonly hybrid rather than purely onchain liquidation. (docs.goldfinch.finance)", "Systemic Risk Exposure High (systemically important liquidity + collateral hub) High (core, long-lived DeFi credit primitive with broad integrations) Very High (DAI is systemically embedded across DeFi and beyond) High (meaningful stablecoin and ETH market integration within Sky ecosystem) (Blockworks) High (rapidly becoming core lending primitive; systemic exposure rises with integration density)": "Medium (systemic footprint lower than Aave/Compound; higher idiosyncratic credit risk)", "Upstream Dependencies DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; oracle networks; stablecoin liquidity; governance/risk stewards Oracles (Chainlink); DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; stablecoin liquidity Oracles; keeper/liquidation infrastructure; governance processes; real-world legal structures (for RWAs) Oracles; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; Sky/Maker liquidity inputs; governance operations (Blockworks) Oracles; liquidator/keeper ecosystem; market curation/allocators; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution": "Offchain underwriting + legal enforcement; stablecoin liquidity; pool participants/backers"}, "source_label": "Lending Markets"}'::jsonb),
