 type (effectively interest rates) Utilization-based IR model (Aave v3 lineage) + custom DAI/sDAI strategies in Spark context (Medium) Market-selected Interest Rate Models (IRMs); IRMs/LLTVs are constrained by governance whitelists (docs.morpho.org)": "Lines of Credit set rates via supply/demand dynamics around target utilization (TrueFi Docs)", "Isolation of Risk Risk primarily at market/reserve parameter level (not isolated per-user); isolation features exist in newer versions/markets but not “isolated pools” by default Moderate isolation: v3 introduces asset isolation via a single base asset with segmented collateral; v2 uses shared pools High isolation at vault-type level; each collateral type has independent parameters Shared pool risk by asset/reserve parameters (not per-market isolation like Morpho Blue) High isolation: each market is isolated and immutable by design (docs.morpho.org)": "Medium isolation: borrower-specific LoCs are isolated; shared risk in some pooled structures depending on product", "Launch Year 2020 (v1 Ethereum mainnet) (aave.com) 2018 (v2 on Ethereum) 2017 (Single-Collateral DAI; Multi-Collateral DAI in 2019) 2023 (public launch May 9, 2023) (X (formerly Twitter)) 2023 (Morpho Blue introduced Oct 2023) (morpho.org)": "2020 (protocol spec era) (GitHub)", "Lending Model Pooled liquidity markets (multi-asset) Pooled liquidity markets (v2); single-collateral base with isolated borrow assets (v3/Comet) CDP / Vault-based collateralized lending Pooled liquidity markets (Aave v3-derived money market) (Spark Docs) Permissionless, isolated lending markets (1 collateral + 1 loan asset per market) (docs.morpho.org)": "Permissioned credit (DAO pools + automated Lines of Credit)", "Liquidation Mechanism Onchain liquidations triggered when Health Factor < 1; liquidators repay debt for collateral + bonus (bonus/thresholds per asset, governance/risk-managed) (aave.com) Onchain liquidations when collateral value breaches borrow limits; liquidators repay debt for collateral at protocol-defined incentives Onchain liquidation via auctions (debt, collateral, surplus); keeper participation required Health Factor-based liquidations (HF < 1), onchain seizure/repay mechanics (Spark Docs) Standard liquidation when LTV exceeds LLTV; liquidators repay debt and seize collateral at discount (protocol-enforced) (docs.morpho.org)": "Default handling includes protocol functions to liquidate bad debt in legacy pools; TRU staking can be slashed up to max liquidation rate to compensate pools (TrueFi Docs)", "Maintaining Organization Aave DAO (governance) + Aave Labs (major dev & interface/operator tooling) (aave.com) Compound DAO (governance) with historical development by Compound Labs MakerDAO (DAO-governed protocol) with core units / contributors maintaining modules Spark Governance (SPK) operating via the Spark Agent in the Sky Atlas (Sky ecosystem) (Spark Docs) Morpho Governance (MORPHO token); governance whitelists IRMs/LLTVs and can activate fee switch (docs.morpho.org)": "TrueFi ecosystem / DAO governance with TRU staking-based risk backstop mechanics documented in TrueFi docs (TrueFi Docs)", "Oracle Dependencies Primarily Chainlink price feeds with protocol risk controls (market-config dependent) Chainlink price feeds (primary), with protocol-defined fallbacks/guards Decentralized Oracle Network (Maker Oracles) with Chainlink integrations and redundancy Oracle-driven risk system; Spark has integrated oracle providers (e.g., RedStone) for lending markets (RedStone blog) Oracle per market; Morpho established an oracle wrapper for Chainlink feeds to support initial markets (morpho.org)": "Chainlink referenced for TRU liquidation pricing in default process writeups (Medium)", "Parameter Control Governance-gated risk parameters + emergency controls (typical DeFi risk-admin pattern) Governance-gated parameters; admin/guardian controls for emergencies (especially during upgrades) Fully governance-controlled parameters; emergency shutdown and circuit breakers exist Parameter updates controlled through governance actions on the Spark Agent (risk, budgets, onboarding, deployments) (Spark Docs) Governance whitelists key risk parameters (LLTVs, IRMs) and can toggle fee switch (capped) (docs.morpho.org)": "Parameters (max liquidation rate, pool terms, managers) are governance-managed; borrower contracts can have upgradeability (per docs) (TrueFi Docs)", "Practitioner Validation Check YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation rules enforced by contracts (HF<1) (aave.com) • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced by contracts • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced via protocol auctions • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation rules enforced (HF<1) (Spark Docs) • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced (LTV>LLTV) (docs.morpho.org) • YES positions unwindable programmatically": "Credit creation: YES (TrueFi Docs) • Liquidation enforcement: YES for protocol mechanics; recovery may be PARTIAL if legal action required (TrueFi Docs) • Programmatic unwind: YES for contract-level state; recovery timelines vary", "Practitioner’s Note Research focus: liquidation mechanics (health factor dynamics), collateral mix concentration, oracle coverage/fallbacks, and governance latency during fast markets. Also track version/market fragmentation (v1 frozen vs v3 active) when analyzing risk. (messari.io) Research focus: differences between v2 and v3 risk profiles; base-asset concentration in v3; liquidation throughput under stress; governance response speed during incidents. Research focus: auction efficiency during stress, oracle latency, RWA exposure and offchain enforcement risk, governance concentration, and emergency shutdown assumptions. Watchpoints: Aave v3 fork deltas (custom DAI/sDAI logic), oracle stack and feed coverage, asset-list governance, and liquidation throughput under stablecoin stress. Also note Spark’s bug bounty posture. (Spark Docs) Watchpoints: oracle selection/config is a first-order risk surface (market-by-market). Validate LLTV choice, oracle robustness, and liquidation liquidity for collateral. Review post-mortems for oracle manipulation and operational incidents. (Morpho Governance Forum)": "Key diligence: (1) borrower upgrade permissions in LoC design, (2) who controls liquidation agents, (3) size/coverage of stkTRU backstop relative to loan book, (4) historical default handling and recovery timing. (TrueFi Docs)", "Primary Role in DeFi Base credit + leverage layer for Ethereum DeFi Base credit layer and leverage primitive for Ethereum DeFi Stablecoin issuance + base credit layer for DeFi DAI-centered credit & liquidity venue; major stablecoin + ETH collateral borrowing/supply rails inside Sky ecosystem (Blockworks) Base lending primitive for permissionless risk markets; “lending infrastructure” others build vaults/allocators on top of": "Onchain credit infrastructure with explicit default/backstop mechanics", "Protocol Status Active (v3 widely used; v1 largely frozen) (messari.io) Active (v3 “Comet” is primary; v2 largely deprecated/frozen for growth) Active (DAI issuance core to Ethereum DeFi) Active Active": "Active (credit rails + lines of credit) (TrueFi Docs)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending; collateralized credit issuance; onchain interest rate mechanics; liquidation + solvency enforced by protocol logic. (aave.com) Meets criteria: issues credit onchain against collateral; defines interest rates, liquidation logic, and solvency rules fully in smart contracts. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing; collateralized credit issuance; explicit liquidation and solvency logic; interest (stability fees) set and enforced onchain. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending, collateralized credit issuance, onchain interest + liquidation + solvency rules. (Spark Docs) Meets criteria: creates credit and enforces liquidation/solvency fully onchain; interest and risk logic are protocol-defined per market. (docs.morpho.org)": "Meets criteria: smart contracts issue credit and track repayments; default mechanics exist onchain (liquidation functions + TRU staking backstop), though some recovery can still involve offchain processes. (TrueFi Docs)", "Systemic Risk Exposure High (systemically important liquidity + collateral hub) High (core, long-lived DeFi credit primitive with broad integrations) Very High (DAI is systemically embedded across DeFi and beyond) High (meaningful stablecoin and ETH market integration within Sky ecosystem) (Blockworks) High (rapidly becoming core lending primitive; systemic exposure rises with integration density)": "Medium–High (less systemic than Aave, but meaningful credit-risk venue)", "Upstream Dependencies DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; oracle networks; stablecoin liquidity; governance/risk stewards Oracles (Chainlink); DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; stablecoin liquidity Oracles; keeper/liquidation infrastructure; governance processes; real-world legal structures (for RWAs) Oracles; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; Sky/Maker liquidity inputs; governance operations (Blockworks) Oracles; liquidator/keeper ecosystem; market curation/allocators; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution": "Offchain borrower assessment + onchain monitoring; governance and staking participation"}, "source_label": "Lending Markets"}'::jsonb),
  ('centrifuge-tinlake-rwa-pools', 'Centrifuge (Tinlake / RWA pools)', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'lending-markets', 'https://centrifuge.io (Centrifuge Docs)', ARRAY['Pool smart contracts issue claims on cashflows', 'financing is deployed to asset originators under pool terms (Gate.com)']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "RWA-focused DeFi credit infrastructure enabling pooled financing against tokenized real-world assets with onchain accounting and tranche structures. (Kraken)", "extras": {"Collateral Types Supported ERC-20s; ETH; widely supports LST collateral in certain markets (risk-parameter dependent) ERC-20s; ETH (wrapped); selected stablecoins; LST support market-dependent (primarily via governance-approved assets) ETH; ERC-20s; selected LSTs; RWAs (via specialized vaults) ERC-20s + ETH (incl. stETH, DAI, sDAI at launch; asset set is governance/risk-managed) (TradingView) ERC-20s; market-defined collateral/loan pairs (including LSTs, stablecoins, and other ERC-20 collateral depending on market config) (docs.morpho.org)": "RWAs tokenized into pool structures; stablecoin funding legs (commonly) (Kraken)", "Dependency Concentration Risk High oracle reliance + large-collateral concentration risk (market-dependent); governance/parameter-change latency risk High oracle reliance; Medium–High asset concentration risk in v3 base asset; governance latency risk High oracle reliance; High governance concentration risk; Medium–High RWA dependency risk High oracle reliance + governance/parameter-change latency risk; asset concentration risk (DAI-centric design) (Spark Docs) High oracle dependence (per-market); configuration/parameter risk; integration/curation risk (markets can be permissionlessly created but quality varies) (mixbytes.io)": "High servicer/originator concentration risk; high offchain enforcement risk; liquidity risk in pool tokens (Gate.com)", "Downstream Consumers Yield strategies, leveraged LPs, hedged carry, structured products, derivatives margin users Yield strategies, leveraged positions, DAO treasuries, arbitrage and carry strategies DEX liquidity, lending protocols, yield strategies, derivatives, DAOs, payment rails Yield strategies, stablecoin allocators, leverage users, structured products integrating DAI liquidity Vaults/allocators, structured lending products, leveraged strategies, institutional deployers using Morpho rails": "RWA allocators, DAO treasuries, structured credit strategies", "Governance Model Token governance (AAVE) via Aave DAO processes; proposals/voting for parameter changes (aave.com) Token governance (COMP) via Compound DAO proposals and voting Token governance (MKR) with executive votes and onchain spell execution Governance via SPK token; Snapshot/signaling and governance system documented by Spark (Spark Docs) Token governance via MORPHO; weighted voting and defined governance powers (docs.morpho.org)": "Governance by CFG holders (onchain governance on Centrifuge Chain; ecosystem direction) (Centrifuge Docs)", "Historical Stress Events Yes (v1 largely frozen/disabled for new supply/borrow; legacy positions remain manageable) (messari.io) Yes (v2 experienced stress events and governance interventions; migration to v3 reflects risk simplification lessons) Yes (notably March 2020 “Black Thursday” auction failures; subsequent mechanism redesigns) No major protocol-loss event cited in core docs; treat as “monitor” (bug bounty active) (Immunefi) Yes (documented oracle-manipulation event on a specific market; plus a frontend-related incident where contracts unaffected) (Morpho Governance Forum)": "Monitor (RWA-specific defaults are more “credit cycle” than oracle-liquidation events)", "Interest Rate Model Utilization-based variable rates; also supports “stable” borrow rate mode (market-specific) Utilization-based interest rate curves per asset (v2); simplified rate model with base/borrow asset separation (v3) Governance-set stability fees per vault type (effectively interest rates) Utilization-based IR model (Aave v3 lineage) + custom DAI/sDAI strategies in Spark context (Medium) Market-selected Interest Rate Models (IRMs); IRMs/LLTVs are constrained by governance whitelists (docs.morpho.org)": "Pool-defined rates and tranche economics (protocol-enforced accounting) (Messari)", "Isolation of Risk Risk primarily at market/reserve parameter level (not isolated per-user); isolation features exist in newer versions/markets but not “isolated pools” by default Moderate isolation: v3 introduces asset isolation via a single base asset with segmented collateral; v2 uses shared pools High isolation at vault-type level; each collateral type has independent parameters Shared pool risk by asset/reserve parameters (not per-market isolation like Morpho Blue) High isolation: each market is isolated and immutable by design (docs.morpho.org)": "High isolation per pool / asset portfolio", "Launch Year 2020 (v1 Ethereum mainnet) (aave.com) 2018 (v2 on Ethereum) 2017 (Single-Collateral DAI; Multi-Collateral DAI in 2019) 2023 (public launch May 9, 2023) (X (formerly Twitter)) 2023 (Morpho Blue introduced Oct 2023) (morpho.org)": "2019 (Tinlake era on Ethereum; later migrations to Centrifuge Chain for some flows) (Gate.com)", "Lending Model Pooled liquidity markets (multi-asset) Pooled liquidity markets (v2); single-collateral base with isolated borrow assets (v3/Comet) CDP / Vault-based collateralized lending Pooled liquidity markets (Aave v3-derived money market) (Spark Docs) Permissionless, isolated lending markets (1 collateral + 1 loan asset per market) (docs.morpho.org)": "Permissioned/curated RWA lending pools (tranches)", "Liquidation Mechanism Onchain liquidations triggered when Health Factor < 1; liquidators repay debt for collateral + bonus (bonus/thresholds per asset, governance/risk-managed) (aave.com) Onchain liquidations when collateral value breaches borrow limits; liquidators repay debt for collateral at protocol-defined incentives Onchain liquidation via auctions (debt, collateral, surplus); keeper participation required Health Factor-based liquidations (HF < 1), onchain seizure/repay mechanics (Spark Docs) Standard liquidation when LTV exceeds LLTV; liquidators repay debt and seize collateral at discount (protocol-enforced) (docs.morpho.org)": "Hybrid: onchain pool accounting + offchain legal enforcement / servicer processes for RWA recovery (Kraken)", "Maintaining Organization Aave DAO (governance) + Aave Labs (major dev & interface/operator tooling) (aave.com) Compound DAO (governance) with historical development by Compound Labs MakerDAO (DAO-governed protocol) with core units / contributors maintaining modules Spark Governance (SPK) operating via the Spark Agent in the Sky Atlas (Sky ecosystem) (Spark Docs) Morpho Governance (MORPHO token); governance whitelists IRMs/LLTVs and can activate fee switch (docs.morpho.org)": "Centrifuge governance (CFG) + Centrifuge org / contributors (protocol + docs) (Centrifuge Docs)", "Oracle Dependencies Primarily Chainlink price feeds with protocol risk controls (market-config dependent) Chainlink price feeds (primary), with protocol-defined fallbacks/guards Decentralized Oracle Network (Maker Oracles) with Chainlink integrations and redundancy Oracle-driven risk system; Spark has integrated oracle providers (e.g., RedStone) for lending markets (RedStone blog) Oracle per market; Morpho established an oracle wrapper for Chainlink feeds to support initial markets (morpho.org)": "Limited vs crypto-collateral lending; depends more on asset reporting/servicing than spot oracles (Gate.com)", "Parameter Control Governance-gated risk parameters + emergency controls (typical DeFi risk-admin pattern) Governance-gated parameters; admin/guardian controls for emergencies (especially during upgrades) Fully governance-controlled parameters; emergency shutdown and circuit breakers exist Parameter updates controlled through governance actions on the Spark Agent (risk, budgets, onboarding, deployments) (Spark Docs) Governance whitelists key risk parameters (LLTVs, IRMs) and can toggle fee switch (capped) (docs.morpho.org)": "Governance-managed pool frameworks + parameters; pool-specific terms set by pool structure (Centrifuge Docs)", "Practitioner Validation Check YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation rules enforced by contracts (HF<1) (aave.com) • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced by contracts • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced via protocol auctions • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation rules enforced (HF<1) (Spark Docs) • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced (LTV>LLTV) (docs.morpho.org) • YES positions unwindable programmatically": "Credit creation: YES • Liquidation enforcement: PARTIAL (often offchain recovery) • Programmatic unwind: PARTIAL (depends on pool liquidity + recovery timelines) (Kraken)", "Practitioner’s Note Research focus: liquidation mechanics (health factor dynamics), collateral mix concentration, oracle coverage/fallbacks, and governance latency during fast markets. Also track version/market fragmentation (v1 frozen vs v3 active) when analyzing risk. (messari.io) Research focus: differences between v2 and v3 risk profiles; base-asset concentration in v3; liquidation throughput under stress; governance response speed during incidents. Research focus: auction efficiency during stress, oracle latency, RWA exposure and offchain enforcement risk, governance concentration, and emergency shutdown assumptions. Watchpoints: Aave v3 fork deltas (custom DAI/sDAI logic), oracle stack and feed coverage, asset-list governance, and liquidation throughput under stablecoin stress. Also note Spark’s bug bounty posture. (Spark Docs) Watchpoints: oracle selection/config is a first-order risk surface (market-by-market). Validate LLTV choice, oracle robustness, and liquidation liquidity for collateral. Review post-mortems for oracle manipulation and operational incidents. (Morpho Governance Forum)": "Key diligence: legal enforceability + jurisdiction, servicer quality, reporting cadence, pool concentration (single-originator risk), and secondary liquidity/exit assumptions. (Gate.com)", "Primary Role in DeFi Base credit + leverage layer for Ethereum DeFi Base credit layer and leverage primitive for Ethereum DeFi Stablecoin issuance + base credit layer for DeFi DAI-centered credit & liquidity venue; major stablecoin + ETH collateral borrowing/supply rails inside Sky ecosystem (Blockworks) Base lending primitive for permissionless risk markets; “lending infrastructure” others build vaults/allocators on top of": "Bridge between DeFi liquidity and real-economy credit (RWA financing rails) (Kraken)", "Protocol Status Active (v3 widely used; v1 largely frozen) (messari.io) Active (v3 “Comet” is primary; v2 largely deprecated/frozen for growth) Active (DAI issuance core to Ethereum DeFi) Active Active": "Active (RWA credit infrastructure; architecture evolved over time) (Gate.com)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending; collateralized credit issuance; onchain interest rate mechanics; liquidation + solvency enforced by protocol logic. (aave.com) Meets criteria: issues credit onchain against collateral; defines interest rates, liquidation logic, and solvency rules fully in smart contracts. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing; collateralized credit issuance; explicit liquidation and solvency logic; interest (stability fees) set and enforced onchain. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending, collateralized credit issuance, onchain interest + liquidation + solvency rules. (Spark Docs) Meets criteria: creates credit and enforces liquidation/solvency fully onchain; interest and risk logic are protocol-defined per market. (docs.morpho.org)": "Creates credit rails via smart-contract pools; repayment/accounting onchain; fits Lending Markets, with liquidation/recovery typically hybrid due to RWAs. (Kraken)", "Systemic Risk Exposure High (systemically important liquidity + collateral hub) High (core, long-lived DeFi credit primitive with broad integrations) Very High (DAI is systemically embedded across DeFi and beyond) High (meaningful stablecoin and ETH market integration within Sky ecosystem) (Blockworks) High (rapidly becoming core lending primitive; systemic exposure rises with integration density)": "Medium (systemic footprint smaller than Aave/Compound; higher idiosyncratic RWA/legal risk)", "Upstream Dependencies DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; oracle networks; stablecoin liquidity; governance/risk stewards Oracles (Chainlink); DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; stablecoin liquidity Oracles; keeper/liquidation infrastructure; governance processes; real-world legal structures (for RWAs) Oracles; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; Sky/Maker liquidity inputs; governance operations (Blockworks) Oracles; liquidator/keeper ecosystem; market curation/allocators; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution": "Offchain asset verification + servicing; stablecoin liquidity; governance/legal wrappers (Gate.com)"}, "source_label": "Lending Markets"}'::jsonb)
) AS v(slug, name, sector_slug, subsector_slug, website, chains, tags, meta)
JOIN public.sectors sec ON sec.slug = v.sector_slug
JOIN public.subsectors s ON s.sector_id = sec.id AND s.slug = v.subsector_slug
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET
  name = EXCLUDED.name,
  subsector_id = EXCLUDED.subsector_id,
  website = EXCLUDED.website,
  chains = EXCLUDED.chains,
  tags = EXCLUDED.tags,
  meta = EXCLUDED.meta,
  updated_at = NOW();
